<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link><description>World News Today: Read the latest world news headlines, Current International breaking news world wide. In depth analysis and top news headlines world wide.</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-11-24T04:17:03+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/296589292.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Tue, 24 Nov 2026 04:17:03 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link></image><item><title><![CDATA['Going to be a better CEO second time around': Jensen Huang returns to Nvidia HQ amid applause and cheers; watch]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136114108.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Jensen Huang returned to Nvidia as CEO after an independent investigation into his alleged extramarital affairs. His reinstatement followed a unanimous decision from Nvidia's board, satisfied with his transparency regarding the issues. Notably, Nvidia's stock surged dramatically, increasing by over 31% in a single day. Meanwhile, the Senate Banking Committee has scheduled a hearing for Huang on December 3.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/going-to-be-a-better-ceo-second-time-around-jensen-huang-returns-to-nvidia-hq-amid-applause-and-cheers-watch/articleshow/136114108.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/going-to-be-a-better-ceo-second-time-around-jensen-huang-returns-to-nvidia-hq-amid-applause-and-cheers-watch/articleshow/136114108.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-24T03:42:05+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Trisha Mahajan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136114170,imgsize-713525.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Indian-origin billionaire Neil Mehta, wife Jash announce $6 million donation to Trump Accounts for San Francisco children]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136113662.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/indian-origin-billionaire-neil-mehta-wife-jash-announce-6-million-donation-to-trump-accounts-for-san-francisco-children/articleshow/136113662.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/indian-origin-billionaire-neil-mehta-wife-jash-announce-6-million-donation-to-trump-accounts-for-san-francisco-children/articleshow/136113662.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-24T01:47:55+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136113673,imgsize-42614.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Ex-Meta engineer who became US citizen and then moved back to Bengaluru after 18 years in America says his children adapted well in India: 'Home is where life takes us']]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136113520.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/ex-meta-engineer-who-became-us-citizen-and-then-moved-back-to-bengaluru-after-18-years-in-america-says-his-children-adapted-well-in-india-home-is-where-life-takes-us/articleshow/136113520.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/ex-meta-engineer-who-became-us-citizen-and-then-moved-back-to-bengaluru-after-18-years-in-america-says-his-children-adapted-well-in-india-home-is-where-life-takes-us/articleshow/136113520.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-24T01:21:10+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136113541,imgsize-102273.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[US flight disruptions: Chicago's O'Hare airport issues brief ground stop over staffing shortage]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136113516.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Chicago’s O'Hare International Airport faced a brief ground stop due to staffing challenges at TRACON, which spanned from 10:40 am to 12:15 pm, coinciding with the Thanksgiving travel rush. This interruption led to the cancellation of approximately twelve flights, with delays averaging 15 minutes. This incident followed a major system glitch at Delta Air Lines, which affected more than 1,000 flights across the country during this peak travel season.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-flight-disruptions-chicagos-ohare-airport-issues-brief-ground-stop-over-staffing-shortage/articleshow/136113516.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-flight-disruptions-chicagos-ohare-airport-issues-brief-ground-stop-over-staffing-shortage/articleshow/136113516.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-24T01:20:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Trisha Mahajan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136113549,imgsize-111366.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Canadian couple went to New Zealand for 14-day vacation, had to spend 14 months as they were jailed when their luggage tag was switched onto a bag carrying meth]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136113342.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/canadian-couple-went-to-new-zealand-for-14-day-vacation-had-to-spend-14-months-as-they-were-jailed-when-their-luggage-tag-was-switched-onto-a-bag-carrying-meth/articleshow/136113342.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/canadian-couple-went-to-new-zealand-for-14-day-vacation-had-to-spend-14-months-as-they-were-jailed-when-their-luggage-tag-was-switched-onto-a-bag-carrying-meth/articleshow/136113342.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-24T00:58:05+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136113370,imgsize-231302.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[New Green Card route proposed by Democrats for immigrants facing deportation in US: Who qualifies and what the bill says]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136111858.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Even if Democrats manage to pass the bill, it would still need President Donald Trump's approval. The president has the power to veto legislation. Trump recently told CBS News' 60 Minutes that he would like to work with Democrats on immigration, although he  reiterated that his administration would maintain a strong enforcement policy and ruled out an agreement that amounted to amnesty]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/new-green-card-route-proposed-by-democrats-for-immigrants-facing-deportation-in-us-who-qualifies-and-what-the-bill-says/articleshow/136111858.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/new-green-card-route-proposed-by-democrats-for-immigrants-facing-deportation-in-us-who-qualifies-and-what-the-bill-says/articleshow/136111858.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-23T23:38:31+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136111921,imgsize-46290.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Michigan couple loses 21-year battle to regain access to jointly owned family land]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136096576.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A Michigan appeals court rejected a couple's attempt to reclaim their share of family property after finding they waited too long to take legal action. Their grandmother had given three grandchildren equal shares in 1992, but a locked gate prevented two of them from accessing the land from 2003.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-michigan-grandmother-gave-three-grandchildren-equal-shares-in-family-property-in-1992-after-one-branch-locked-a-gate-in-2003-judges-ruled-the-others-waited-too-long-to-reclaim-their-stake/articleshow/136096576.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-michigan-grandmother-gave-three-grandchildren-equal-shares-in-family-property-in-1992-after-one-branch-locked-a-gate-in-2003-judges-ruled-the-others-waited-too-long-to-reclaim-their-stake/articleshow/136096576.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-24T03:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136098027,imgsize-77374.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Mother sues summer camp after 9-year-old son drowns in swimming pool]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136101117.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The family of nine-year-old King Sha'Mar Overton has filed a $100 million wrongful-death lawsuit against Virginia summer camp SwimRVA after he drowned on his first day at the facility. His mother alleges that staff knew he could not swim but allowed him into the pool without adequate supervision.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/family-of-nine-year-old-king-shamar-overton-filed-a-100-million-wrongful-death-lawsuit-after-he-drowned-at-a-virginia-summer-camp-alleges-the-camp-allowed-him-into-a-swimming-pool-despite-knowing-he-couldnt-swim/articleshow/136101117.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/family-of-nine-year-old-king-shamar-overton-filed-a-100-million-wrongful-death-lawsuit-after-he-drowned-at-a-virginia-summer-camp-alleges-the-camp-allowed-him-into-a-swimming-pool-despite-knowing-he-couldnt-swim/articleshow/136101117.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-24T03:50:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136101513,imgsize-211296.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Michigan woman challenges $180,000 foreclosure after deed wrongly cut her home redemption period to six months]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136097448.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Cynthia Zalewski inherited her mother's home but faced foreclosure after missing payments during the pandemic. The sheriff's deed erroneously stated she had six months instead of twelve to redeem the property. The Michigan Court of Appeals recognized this error as a significant irregularity in the foreclosure process. However, Zalewski must show how the mistake prejudiced her ability to reclaim her home.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-michigan-woman-inherited-her-mothers-home-in-2013-but-it-sold-at-foreclosure-for-about-180000-after-a-deed-gave-her-six-months-to-redeem-instead-of-the-12-required-by-law-a-november-20-appeal-revived-her-claim/articleshow/136097448.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-michigan-woman-inherited-her-mothers-home-in-2013-but-it-sold-at-foreclosure-for-about-180000-after-a-deed-gave-her-six-months-to-redeem-instead-of-the-12-required-by-law-a-november-20-appeal-revived-her-claim/articleshow/136097448.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-24T02:58:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136097560,imgsize-2050496.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Sri Lankan man loses £7 million claim after footage exposes false injury claims]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136097213.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/a-sri-lankan-man-sought-over-7-million-from-the-uk-home-office-for-alleged-detention-injuries-surveillance-footage-showed-him-carrying-out-daily-activities-and-the-high-court-found-his-claim-fundamentally-dishonest/articleshow/136097213.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/a-sri-lankan-man-sought-over-7-million-from-the-uk-home-office-for-alleged-detention-injuries-surveillance-footage-showed-him-carrying-out-daily-activities-and-the-high-court-found-his-claim-fundamentally-dishonest/articleshow/136097213.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-24T02:50:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136097384,imgsize-132385.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Australian court orders bamboo hedge trimmed after neighbours' property dispute]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136096822.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A legal battle arose between Leonard Clyde Lloyd and Susan Boyd Valstar over a bamboo hedge in Australia. The Land and Environment Court ordered the removal of bamboo growing on the boundary. Lloyd's complaints included property damage and reduced sunlight due to the bamboo's height. The court ruled that vegetation contributed minimally to fence damage and ordered equal cost sharing for its replacement.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/a-16-metre-bamboo-hedge-sparked-an-australian-neighbours-fight-over-a-damaged-fence-blocked-gutters-and-lost-sunlight-on-november-19-a-court-ordered-removal-within-one-metre-and-split-fence-costs-equally/articleshow/136096822.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/a-16-metre-bamboo-hedge-sparked-an-australian-neighbours-fight-over-a-damaged-fence-blocked-gutters-and-lost-sunlight-on-november-19-a-court-ordered-removal-within-one-metre-and-split-fence-costs-equally/articleshow/136096822.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-24T01:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136096928,imgsize-1082523.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[15,000-year-old seal-tooth pendant reveals ancient human connections in Britain]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5p