-of-the-lawsuit/articleshow/136096573.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/female-physician-assistants-at-michigan-medicine-allegedly-earned-9000-less-a-year-than-male-colleagues-on-november-20-appeals-judges-allowed-newer-equal-pay-claims-to-proceed-while-barring-older-parts-of-the-lawsuit/articleshow/136096573.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-24T00:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136096727,imgsize-1758662.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[California father drops lawsuit after son's AI-flagged essay leads to a D grade]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136095334.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-california-students-essay-was-flagged-76-ai-generated-by-turnitin-his-father-sued-the-school-after-a-supervised-rewrite-earned-a-d-and-lowered-his-final-grade-to-a-c-but-later-dropped-the-case/articleshow/136095334.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-california-students-essay-was-flagged-76-ai-generated-by-turnitin-his-father-sued-the-school-after-a-supervised-rewrite-earned-a-d-and-lowered-his-final-grade-to-a-c-but-later-dropped-the-case/articleshow/136095334.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-24T00:50:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136095548,imgsize-1134399.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Executor Challenge Fails: Court rejects daughter’s bid over speculative debt; brother remains executor]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136106900.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-pennsylvania-mother-left-her-real-estate-to-one-son-and-the-rest-of-her-estate-to-a-church-while-a-218891-state-care-claim-was-settled-for-about-40000-a-daughters-bid-to-remove-the-executor-has-failed/articleshow/136106900.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-pennsylvania-mother-left-her-real-estate-to-one-son-and-the-rest-of-her-estate-to-a-church-while-a-218891-state-care-claim-was-settled-for-about-40000-a-daughters-bid-to-remove-the-executor-has-failed/articleshow/136106900.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-23T23:56:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136107034,imgsize-69763.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[British couple win £1,488 after using AI to fight housing eviction]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136095855.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A British couple in their 70s who fought eviction from their home have won the right to recover £1,488 spent on an AI legal research tool. The High Court allowed the expense after finding that the subscription was purchased specifically to help them prepare their case without legal representation. The couple had challenged a housing association's electricity charges, which had formed the basis of possession proceedings.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/a-british-couple-in-their-70s-fought-eviction-from-a-housing-association-flat-over-electricity-charges-after-winning-their-appeal-a-high-court-judge-allowed-1488-they-had-borrowed-for-ai-assisted-legal-research/articleshow/136095855.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/a-british-couple-in-their-70s-fought-eviction-from-a-housing-association-flat-over-electricity-charges-after-winning-their-appeal-a-high-court-judge-allowed-1488-they-had-borrowed-for-ai-assisted-legal-research/articleshow/136095855.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-23T23:53:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136096348,imgsize-135740.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[UK hotel worker loses court claims; booked a 4-week holiday without permission]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136093358.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Dylan Forster, an employee at Inn on the Lake, unilaterally booked a trip to South Africa, despite not receiving permission for a four-week leave due to hotel policies and staffing requirements. Upon resigning, he raised grievances about discrimination and injury. However, an employment tribunal concluded that his claims were baseless, confirming the hotel's adherence to its protocols and reasonable actions.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/a-uk-hotel-worker-booked-a-four-week-holiday-without-his-managers-permission-then-took-his-employer-to-a-tribunal-over-discrimination-and-unfair-dismissal-the-judge-rejected-all-his-claims/articleshow/136093358.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/a-uk-hotel-worker-booked-a-four-week-holiday-without-his-managers-permission-then-took-his-employer-to-a-tribunal-over-discrimination-and-unfair-dismissal-the-judge-rejected-all-his-claims/articleshow/136093358.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-23T23:50:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136093454,imgsize-967378.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 2010, Nebraska couple financed $100,000 building sale; buyer defaulted in 2012, court upheld $247,068 foreclosure]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136094717.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a significant legal decision, the Nebraska Supreme Court ruled on a foreclosure case involving RCTS Properties, which failed to fulfill payments on a seller-financed loan. The court clarified that the timeline for foreclosure wasn't impacted by bankruptcy filings or claims. It emphasized a 10-year limit for such actions, rejecting the buyer's assertions and allowing the property's sale if the outstanding amount stayed unpaid.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2010-a-nebraska-couple-financed-100000-of-a-building-sale-after-the-buyer-stopped-paying-in-2012-the-state-supreme-court-upheld-foreclosure-in-2026-on-a-lien-that-grew-to-247068/articleshow/136094717.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2010-a-nebraska-couple-financed-100000-of-a-building-sale-after-the-buyer-stopped-paying-in-2012-the-state-supreme-court-upheld-foreclosure-in-2026-on-a-lien-that-grew-to-247068/articleshow/136094717.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-23T23:04:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136094793,imgsize-1956171.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Sculptor Chester Beach's Brewster estate 'OldWalls' hits market for $4.15M]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136099718.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[OldWalls, a historic estate in Brewster, New York, is now available for $4.15 million. This 10.49-acre property features a main house with eight bedrooms and six and a half bathrooms. The estate was originally built by sculptor Chester Beach and has been carefully maintained over the years. It includes multiple buildings and amenities suitable for equestrian use. Potential buyers are those seeking privacy while remaining close to New York City.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/a-new-york-sculptor-built-a-stone-estate-in-1917-and-worked-there-for-decades-leaving-behind-his-studio-and-art-filled-buildings-a-century-later-the-10-49-acre-oldwalls-is-seeking-a-new-owner-for-4-15-million/articleshow/136099718.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/a-new-york-sculptor-built-a-stone-estate-in-1917-and-worked-there-for-decades-leaving-behind-his-studio-and-art-filled-buildings-a-century-later-the-10-49-acre-oldwalls-is-seeking-a-new-owner-for-4-15-million/articleshow/136099718.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-23T23:02:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Real Estate Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-136099801,imgsize-409114.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Florida scientists use GPS-collared opossums to track hidden pythons]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/136089905.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/opossums-wearing-gps-collars-are-helping-florida-scientists-find-hidden-burmese-pythons-when-a-collar-goes-still-for-four-hours-and-then-starts-moving-again-a-snake-may-have-swallowed-the-animal/articleshow/136089905.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/opossums-wearing-gps-collars-are-helping-florida-scientists-find-hidden-burmese-pythons-when-a-collar-goes-still-for-four-hours-and-then-starts-moving-again-a-snake-may-have-swallowed-the-animal/articleshow/1360899